# Copy to .env and fill in ONE key. .env is gitignored.
#
#   cp .env.example .env
#   open -e .env
#
# Lines starting with # are ignored. The two lines below are NOT commented,
# which is deliberate: this file should work as soon as a key is pasted in.

LLM_PROVIDER=groq
GROQ_API_KEY=
GEMINI_API_KEY=
CEREBRAS_API_KEY=

# Get a key at console.groq.com. Free, no card, no expiry.
#
# Groq is the default because it is still free without a card. The binding limit is
# 200,000 tokens a day, which is about two full self-test runs. Exhaust it and every
# clause comes back unread, so pace your testing across the day or use --offline,
# which needs no provider at all.
#
# LLM_PROVIDER=gemini is the better free option for volume. aistudio.google.com,
# free, no card, and the limit is counted in requests rather than tokens, which
# suits one-call-per-clause work far better than a daily token ceiling.
#
# LLM_PROVIDER=cerebras is here but is no longer free. Cerebras ended its no-card
# free tier on 17 August 2026; new accounts get 5 dollars of credit that expires in
# 30 days and needs a payment method. Many comparison articles still describe the
# old tier. Kept working for anyone who has credit.
#
# Every key can sit here at once. Only LLM_PROVIDER decides which is used.
#
# Other providers. Change LLM_PROVIDER above to switch, and leave the spare keys
# here as a fallback. Only LLM_PROVIDER decides which one is used.
#
#   gemini      aistudio.google.com, free, lower rate limit
#   anthropic   console.anthropic.com, prepaid credits
#   ollama      runs locally, no key, no network
#
# GEMINI_API_KEY=
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=

# Calls per minute. Defaults are conservative per provider; lower this if you get
# rate limited during a corpus scan.
# LLM_RPM=

# Pin a model if the default has been retired. See: python src/llm.py --list
# LLM_MODEL=
